WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:01.920
You may have heard
the expression

00:00:01.920 --> 00:00:03.760
“knowledge is power.”

00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:06.640
Well, today we’re going
to give you more power

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:08.400
to control your
diet and lifestyle

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:10.480
by giving you the facts.

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:13.280
Welcome to the
Nutrition Facts Podcast.

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:15.920
I’m your host,
Dr. Michael Greger.

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:18.960
It’s time for the Nutrition
Facts Grab Bag

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:22.000
where we look at the science
on a wide variety of topics.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:24.480
Today we start with
a pressing question:

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:28.880
why don’t health insurers
embrace plant-based eating?

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:31.680
Many of the diseases that
cause a constant drain

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:35.840
on health care budgets can be
prevented by proper nutrition.

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:39.120
So why aren't the big
payors getting involved?

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:42.640
I mean, even like a 1% decline
in excess body fat could

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:45.280
alone save tens of billions.

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:49.280
You'd think at least the health
insurance industry would try

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:51.920
to get people to eat healthier
to try to pay out less money.

00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:57.920
Well, one could say the insurance
industry actually benefits from

00:00:57.920 --> 00:01:01.200
high health care costs because
these rising costs are simply

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:03.840
passed on to both individuals
and employers in terms of

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:07.680
higher premiums, and
insurers take a fixed percentage

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:09.920
of these premiums
as increasing profits.

00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:14.320
They get a piece of the pie,
so the bigger the pie —

00:01:14.320 --> 00:01:17.920
the unhealthier everyone is —
the bigger their piece.

00:01:18.560 --> 00:01:22.080
As such, insurers have not
done as much as they could

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:25.120
to help reduce health care
costs because lower costs

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:27.200
would hurt their bottom line.

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:31.680
What if there was a medication
that could successfully treat

00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:34.920
and even reverse heart disease,
type 2 diabetes, high blood pressure,

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:39.040
and many other chronic conditions
without any negative side effects and

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:41.920
offered the promise of dramatically
reduced health care costs?

00:01:42.880 --> 00:01:45.840
Imagine all the advertising
there would be to promote it.

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:47.760
Imagine how much
they would charge.

00:01:47.760 --> 00:01:50.560
A drug that could not just
treat but cure diabetes

00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:51.600
and these other diseases?

00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:56.000
Then what if you were told
that medication exists today,

00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:00.240
is available to everyone in
unlimited quantities at a low cost,

00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:03.520
but the vast majority of the American
public has never heard about it.

00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:08.400
You want a solution to significantly
reduce health care costs?

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:12.720
The solution is to use food
as medical treatment,

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:17.040
specifically foods made from
minimally processed plants.

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:21.440
One of the main barriers is simply
the current widespread belief

00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:23.760
that once someone has
a chronic condition,

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:26.000
such as heart disease,
type 2 diabetes,

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:29.280
there's very little that can be done
to actually reverse the disease,

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:33.040
and the best outcome possible
is to maintain the condition

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:35.920
so that it just
doesn't get any worse.

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:38.160
The fact that a whole food
plant-based approach provides

00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:42.000
a safe, effective, low-cost alternative
to not just eliminating symptoms

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:45.200
but potentially reversing
the underlying condition

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:46.880
without drugs or surgery

00:02:46.880 --> 00:02:49.760
is unknown to a vast
majority of Americans.

00:02:49.760 --> 00:02:53.520
In contrast to the pharmaceutical
industry that spends large sums

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:57.040
to market new drugs, there are
not big profits in promoting

00:02:57.040 --> 00:02:58.320
a plant-based diet.

00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:03.760
The politics surrounding healthcare
is who's going to pay for it,

00:03:03.760 --> 00:03:07.280
instead of what kind
of healthcare is best?

00:03:07.280 --> 00:03:10.560
And the evidence is overwhelming
that a whole food, plant-based diet

00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:14.160
provides the best opportunity to not
only reduce the growth in spending,

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:18.160
but actually decrease total health
care costs more than any drug,

00:03:18.160 --> 00:03:22.400
medical procedure, insurance reform,
or provider payment model out there.

00:03:23.440 --> 00:03:26.480
Thankfully, the word is spreading.

00:03:26.480 --> 00:03:29.600
A review of the evidence published
in Kaiser Permanente's journal

00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:32.080
concluded that physicians should
consider recommending

00:03:32.080 --> 00:03:35.520
a plant-based diet to all their
patients, especially those

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:38.720
with high blood pressure, diabetes,
cardiovascular disease, or obesity.

00:03:39.680 --> 00:03:42.800
Kaiser has followed up
with user friendly guides

00:03:42.800 --> 00:03:44.080
(freely available online)

00:03:44.080 --> 00:03:46.800
for both physicians and patients,
explaining the benefits

00:03:46.800 --> 00:03:50.720
and practical aspects of
implementing a plant-based diet.

00:03:50.720 --> 00:03:54.640
So hey, why aren't all insurers
sending out such information

00:03:54.640 --> 00:03:55.600
to all their members?

00:03:56.720 --> 00:03:59.520
You know how all the
drug ads are like,

00:03:59.520 --> 00:04:02.080
"Ask your doctor if this
drug is right for you."

00:04:02.080 --> 00:04:06.000
Well, members could be
prompted to ask their physicians

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:10.000
about the ability of plant-based
diets to reduce or eliminate

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:12.320
prescription drug use,
reverse disease.

00:04:12.880 --> 00:04:15.360
Though, of course, these
materials would also have

00:04:15.360 --> 00:04:18.720
to list all the side effects.
Side effects include

00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:22.160
increased energy, lower blood
pressure, improved digestion,

00:04:22.160 --> 00:04:25.120
all while eating unlimited
quantities of satisfying food.

00:04:25.120 --> 00:04:30.933
Ask your doctor if
plants are right for you.

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:33.360
Did you know that
there is little guarantee

00:04:33.360 --> 00:04:36.240
that a dietary supplement
will actually contain

00:04:36.240 --> 00:04:38.720
what's advertised
on the packaging?

00:04:38.720 --> 00:04:40.480
Here’s the story.

00:04:40.480 --> 00:04:44.720
In a video I did a few years ago,
I talked about how press releases

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:48.240
about the latest science coming
out of even top medical centers

00:04:48.240 --> 00:04:50.880
were filled with
overstatements and omissions.

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:54.880
Medical journal press releases
suffered from similar problems,

00:04:54.880 --> 00:04:57.520
and press releases from the
drug companies themselves

00:04:57.520 --> 00:05:00.880
were no different, filled with
hype and exaggeration.

00:05:01.600 --> 00:05:04.960
What about press releases
issued by the supplements industry?

00:05:05.520 --> 00:05:07.600
Not even the companies
that published the studies,

00:05:07.600 --> 00:05:09.040
but like trade organizations

00:05:09.040 --> 00:05:12.720
for the multi-billion-dollar
dietary supplement industry?

00:05:13.360 --> 00:05:18.880
Researchers found that 100% of
supplements industry press releases

00:05:18.880 --> 00:05:23.360
contained "spin," meaning strategies
to hype or denigrate findings

00:05:23.360 --> 00:05:25.680
to distort the results
of clinical studies.

00:05:26.480 --> 00:05:30.160
And here's the crazy part:
industry press releases advocated

00:05:30.160 --> 00:05:32.320
supplement use in response
to more than 90%

00:05:32.960 --> 00:05:36.480
of even the studies that
reported no benefit or harm.

00:05:37.040 --> 00:05:38.320
Here are the harm studies.

00:05:38.960 --> 00:05:41.920
A study comes out showing a
supplement is actually bad for you,

00:05:41.920 --> 00:05:44.640
and the vast majority of
independent institutions like

00:05:44.640 --> 00:05:47.600
the National Institutes of Health
or mainstream media stories

00:05:47.600 --> 00:05:51.840
are like "don't take it."
Duh. But the industry trade

00:05:51.840 --> 00:05:56.240
organizations are like, "Harm?
Go for it! Buy an extra bottle."

00:05:56.240 --> 00:05:59.360
It is, therefore, likely that the
propagation of the spin-enriched

00:05:59.360 --> 00:06:03.120
industry press releases contributes
to the ongoing, and even burgeoning,

00:06:03.120 --> 00:06:07.120
enthusiasm for use of supplements
in the face of accumulating evidence

00:06:07.120 --> 00:06:10.880
of most of their ineffectiveness
and, in some cases, harm.

00:06:11.680 --> 00:06:15.200
In some cases, people are paying
to make themselves sick.

00:06:16.080 --> 00:06:19.840
Sadly, the science may not even
matter to many supplement users.

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:24.560
Most dietary supplement users said
that they would be minimally influenced

00:06:24.560 --> 00:06:27.920
by independent, taxpayer-funded
studies contradicting

00:06:27.920 --> 00:06:30.960
the efficacy claims of
supplement manufacturers.

00:06:30.960 --> 00:06:34.320
Only a minority of users said they
would stop taking a supplement

00:06:34.320 --> 00:06:37.840
if public health authorities stated
that it was just a waste of money.

00:06:38.640 --> 00:06:44.400
The iconic image of the snake oil
salesman was actually a real dude:

00:06:44.400 --> 00:06:48.560
Clark "the Rattlesnake King" Stanley
in 1916.

00:06:49.120 --> 00:06:54.000
Turns out that Stanley's snake oil,
in fact, contained no snake oil at all

00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:57.840
but rather just like spicy
mothballs and turpentine,

00:06:57.840 --> 00:07:01.360
prosecuted under the newly enacted
Pure Food and Drug Act,

00:07:01.360 --> 00:07:05.120
and ultimately fined a
lofty sum of $20 bucks.

00:07:06.160 --> 00:07:10.560
And a century later, here we are
with snake oil coming out our ears,

00:07:10.560 --> 00:07:15.280
a vast number of supplements marketed
and sold without routine oversight.

00:07:15.280 --> 00:07:18.080
Now, the supplement industry
bristles at such talk, saying that

00:07:18.080 --> 00:07:21.760
the supplement industry is
regulated to protect consumers.

00:07:21.760 --> 00:07:25.200
And it's true there are definitely
laws on the books, but the ability

00:07:25.200 --> 00:07:28.960
of regulators to successfully carry
out this mission is hampered

00:07:28.960 --> 00:07:31.360
by the sheer number of products.

00:07:31.360 --> 00:07:35.040
The FDA estimates there are more
than 85,000 dietary supplement

00:07:35.040 --> 00:07:37.760
products currently available
in the U.S. alone.

00:07:37.760 --> 00:07:41.520
So there's the sheer number,
the under reporting of adverse

00:07:41.520 --> 00:07:44.640
side effects, the difficulty
of successfully prosecuting

00:07:44.640 --> 00:07:47.840
cases against offenders,
and the ease with which

00:07:47.840 --> 00:07:50.960
suppliers can rebrand products
removed from the shelves

00:07:50.960 --> 00:07:54.720
have led to a largely
unregulated environment.

00:07:54.720 --> 00:07:57.360
In the real world, there is little
guarantee that a supplement

00:07:57.360 --> 00:08:00.720
will even contain what is
advertised on the packaging and

00:08:00.720 --> 00:08:04.720
not contain unlisted ingredients,
potentially leading to significant

00:08:04.720 --> 00:08:09.520
harms, resulting in an estimated
23,000 ER visits every year.

00:08:10.160 --> 00:08:14.480
Now, of course, prescription drugs
don't just sicken but kill many more,

00:08:14.480 --> 00:08:17.520
making them perhaps the
third leading cause of death,

00:08:17.520 --> 00:08:21.200
wiping out more than
100,000 Americans, but still,

00:08:21.200 --> 00:08:24.000
the less death and disability,
the better.

00:08:24.800 --> 00:08:26.880
Dietary supplements
are often adulterated

00:08:26.880 --> 00:08:29.440
with undeclared pharmaceuticals,
which could represent

00:08:29.440 --> 00:08:33.760
an enormous risk to consumers, most
often found in erectile dysfunction,

00:08:33.760 --> 00:08:36.560
weight loss, diabetes, and high
blood pressure supplements.

00:08:37.280 --> 00:08:39.200
But wait a second.
What about

00:08:39.200 --> 00:08:42.400
supplement manufacturers
who say they have independent,

00:08:42.400 --> 00:08:44.800
third-party certification of purity?

00:08:45.680 --> 00:08:49.920
There is a practice called
"dry labbing," a dirty little secret

00:08:49.920 --> 00:08:53.040
of the supplements industry,
where quality assurance labs

00:08:53.040 --> 00:08:55.600
just rubber stamp fake documents.

00:08:55.600 --> 00:09:00.560
And if you think that's outrageous,
check out the story of BMPEA.

00:09:01.680 --> 00:09:05.840
A researcher at Harvard published
a paper replicating prior research

00:09:05.840 --> 00:09:10.240
from the FDA detecting a designer
amphetamine-like stimulant,

00:09:10.800 --> 00:09:12.560
beta-methylphenylethylamine,

00:09:12.560 --> 00:09:16.080
in various U.S. supplements
sold in the United States.

00:09:16.080 --> 00:09:19.600
In response, one of the offenders,
Hi-Tech Pharmaceuticals,

00:09:19.600 --> 00:09:21.920
manufacturers of weight
loss supplements like

00:09:21.920 --> 00:09:24.080
Black Widow and Yellow Scorpion,

00:09:24.640 --> 00:09:28.080
sued the Harvard researcher
for libel, slander, and product

00:09:28.080 --> 00:09:33.280
disparagement, originally to the
tune of $200 million in damages.

00:09:34.240 --> 00:09:36.960
This was all documented
in a piece by STAT,

00:09:37.680 --> 00:09:39.920
which is an excellent source
of medical journalism

00:09:39.920 --> 00:09:40.720
that I recommend.

00:09:41.840 --> 00:09:44.560
The head of Hi-Tech openly
admitted that he was

00:09:44.560 --> 00:09:47.280
"hoping that we were
able to silence this guy."

00:09:47.280 --> 00:09:51.760
And while ultimately unsuccessful in
court, Hi-Tech's lawsuit effectively

00:09:51.760 --> 00:09:54.080
sent a warning to other researchers.

00:09:54.080 --> 00:09:56.480
In fact, Hi-Tech's CEO is
attributed as saying,

00:09:56.480 --> 00:10:00.400
he "hope[s] that the long and costly
legal battle will scare away

00:10:00.400 --> 00:10:05.522
other academics from investigating
the supplement industry."

00:10:06.320 --> 00:10:08.240
Finally today, we
discover that those

00:10:08.240 --> 00:10:10.640
who are eating
plant-based diets

00:10:10.640 --> 00:10:15.207
have a reduced load of antibiotic
resistance genes in their gut.

00:10:16.320 --> 00:10:20.240
There are nearly a million salmonella
and campylobacter infections

00:10:20.240 --> 00:10:24.080
in children 10 and younger
each year in the United States.

00:10:24.080 --> 00:10:28.240
Some of these infections are severe,
causing meningitis and death, and

00:10:28.240 --> 00:10:32.240
requiring treatment with antibiotics.
The problem is that there's

00:10:32.240 --> 00:10:35.520
an increasing problem of
antibiotic resistance among

00:10:35.520 --> 00:10:38.160
these bugs that threatens
our ability to treat them.

00:10:38.800 --> 00:10:42.960
Part of the problem is that the same
life-saving miracle-drug antibiotics

00:10:42.960 --> 00:10:45.280
are being squandered
for use in food animals

00:10:45.280 --> 00:10:47.120
for things like growth promotion

00:10:47.120 --> 00:10:49.600
in such unhygienic,
crowded conditions,

00:10:49.600 --> 00:10:52.480
which increases the likelihood
that pathogens like salmonella

00:10:52.480 --> 00:10:54.640
or campylobacter will
become resistant.

00:10:54.800 --> 00:10:58.400
But there's another problem.
The resistance determinants,

00:10:58.400 --> 00:11:01.360
the genes that encode
antibiotic resistance,

00:11:02.000 --> 00:11:06.080
may be transmitted from food animals
to humans through the food supply.

00:11:06.080 --> 00:11:10.080
See, most resistant bacteria
have mobile genetic elements,

00:11:10.080 --> 00:11:12.960
like these little circles
of DNA called plasmids,

00:11:12.960 --> 00:11:16.160
that carry the resistance genes
that they can then pass on

00:11:16.160 --> 00:11:19.600
to other bacteria, including
those in our own gut.

00:11:20.480 --> 00:11:23.760
Food animals are, therefore,
a reservoir of antibiotic resistance

00:11:23.760 --> 00:11:26.400
genes and a potential
vector for transmission

00:11:26.400 --> 00:11:30.160
of antibiotic resistance genes to
the human intestinal microbiome.

00:11:30.720 --> 00:11:34.160
In this study, transfer of an
antibiotic resistance plasmid

00:11:34.160 --> 00:11:37.280
from an E. coli originating
from a chicken raised for meat

00:11:37.280 --> 00:11:40.640
to human gut bugs was
assessed by using a model

00:11:40.640 --> 00:11:46.640
that mimics the human intestines.
And it happened within two hours.

00:11:47.520 --> 00:11:51.760
This spread of antibiotic resistance
genes presents an alarming scenario,

00:11:51.760 --> 00:11:55.840
a growing concern that antibiotic
resistant bacteria present on food

00:11:55.840 --> 00:12:01.120
can transfer their resistance genes
to the inherent gut microbiome

00:12:01.120 --> 00:12:02.640
of the consumer.

00:12:02.640 --> 00:12:07.040
But you don't know
until you put it to the test.

00:12:07.600 --> 00:12:14.080
Assessing antibiotic resistance
gene loads in vegan vs. vegetarian

00:12:14.080 --> 00:12:16.400
vs. omnivore gut bacteria.

00:12:17.680 --> 00:12:20.400
You'd think the results
might be obvious,

00:12:20.400 --> 00:12:22.720
but antibiotic resistance
genes are spread due to

00:12:22.720 --> 00:12:26.880
manure application on agricultural
fields of fruits and vegetables.

00:12:26.880 --> 00:12:30.160
Yes, massive antibiotic use in
animal farming is considered

00:12:30.160 --> 00:12:33.520
as the greatest contributor to the
presence of antibiotic-resistant

00:12:33.520 --> 00:12:37.520
bacteria in food of animal origin:
meats, eggs, and dairy.

00:12:37.520 --> 00:12:40.800
Nevertheless, sewage from
treated animals may impact

00:12:40.800 --> 00:12:43.200
on vegetables grown
on fertilized fields,

00:12:44.000 --> 00:12:47.120
but it was largely unknown
whether, and to what extent,

00:12:47.120 --> 00:12:50.320
antibiotic-resistant bacteria are
being transferred to vegetables

00:12:50.320 --> 00:12:54.400
and then to the human gut until now.

00:12:55.040 --> 00:12:58.560
Researchers looked for antibiotic-
resistant genes against sulfa drugs

00:12:58.560 --> 00:13:02.320
like bactrim, tetracyclines,
penicillins and cephalosporins,

00:13:02.320 --> 00:13:04.800
and streptomycin-type antibiotics

00:13:04.800 --> 00:13:09.200
and both omnivores and vegetarians
showed a signigicantly higher

00:13:09.200 --> 00:13:11.920
antibiotic-resistant
gene load in their guts

00:13:11.920 --> 00:13:14.080
as compared with vegans.

00:13:14.080 --> 00:13:17.360
There wasn't a significant difference
between omnivores and vegetarians,

00:13:17.360 --> 00:13:20.800
but significantly lower loads in
vegans compared to omnivores,

00:13:20.800 --> 00:13:24.720
and vegans compared to
vegetarians, the first evidence

00:13:24.720 --> 00:13:26.800
that a vegan lifestyle
is associated with

00:13:26.800 --> 00:13:30.240
a reduced load of human
gut antibiotic-resistant genes,

00:13:30.240 --> 00:13:31.200
but not the last.

00:13:31.760 --> 00:13:34.880
Fewer tetracycline resistance
genes in vegan guts and

00:13:34.880 --> 00:13:39.280
more vancomycin resistance genes
in the guts of those who eat meat.

00:13:39.280 --> 00:13:41.600
No surprise, since they found
a correlation between

00:13:41.600 --> 00:13:43.440
tetracycline resistance genes

00:13:43.440 --> 00:13:46.320
and the intake of eggs,
milk, and cheese ---

00:13:46.320 --> 00:13:49.360
I like how there are so many
types of milk these days

00:13:49.360 --> 00:13:52.240
they have to specify
"milk from animal sources."

00:13:53.200 --> 00:13:55.760
And a higher incidence of
vancomycin resistance genes

00:13:55.760 --> 00:13:59.520
was found in consumers
of eggs, poultry, fish, and seafood.

00:13:59.520 --> 00:14:03.600
And vancomycin is one of our
antibiotics of last resort, used to

00:14:03.600 --> 00:14:06.720
treat serious life-threatening
strep and staph infections

00:14:06.720 --> 00:14:08.480
like MRSA (M-R-S-A).

00:14:09.200 --> 00:14:12.080
Despite the links to dairy and
eggs, just cutting out meat

00:14:12.080 --> 00:14:15.360
has indeed been shown to offer
an advantage in some studies,

00:14:15.360 --> 00:14:19.680
as bacteria obtained from meat-eater
poop samples showed resistance

00:14:19.680 --> 00:14:22.560
to a greater number of antibiotics
and carried more tested

00:14:22.560 --> 00:14:28.878
antibiotic resistance genes compared
to the vegan or vegetarian poop.

00:14:29.120 --> 00:14:32.080
We would love it if you could
share with us your stories

00:14:32.080 --> 00:14:35.360
about reinventing your health
through evidence-based nutrition.

00:14:35.360 --> 00:14:38.000
Go to nutritionfacts.org/testimonials.

00:14:38.000 --> 00:14:41.200
We may share it on our social
media to help inspire others.

00:14:41.760 --> 00:14:45.440
To see any graphs, charts, graphics,
images, or studies mentioned here,

00:14:45.440 --> 00:14:48.720
please go to the Nutrition Facts
Podcast landing page.

00:14:48.720 --> 00:14:51.320
There you’ll find all the
detailed information you need –

00:14:51.320 --> 00:14:55.440
plus, links to all of the sources
we cite for each of these topics.

00:14:56.320 --> 00:14:59.600
For a timely text on the
pathogens that cause pandemics,

00:15:00.320 --> 00:15:02.480
order the e-book,
audiobook, or hard copy

00:15:02.480 --> 00:15:05.360
of my last book,
“How to Survive a Pandemic”.

00:15:06.080 --> 00:15:09.520
For recipes, check out
my second-to-last book,

00:15:09.520 --> 00:15:12.320
my “How Not to Diet Cookbook”.

00:15:12.320 --> 00:15:14.960
It’s beautifully designed
with more than 100 recipes

00:15:14.960 --> 00:15:17.120
for delicious and
nutritious meals.

00:15:17.680 --> 00:15:19.760
And all the proceeds
I receive from the sales

00:15:19.760 --> 00:15:22.160
of all my books goes to charity.

00:15:22.880 --> 00:15:26.240
NutritionFacts.org is a nonprofit,
science-based public service,

00:15:26.240 --> 00:15:28.400
where you can sign up
for free daily updates

00:15:28.400 --> 00:15:32.720
on the latest in nutrition research
via bite-sized videos and articles.

00:15:33.600 --> 00:15:35.680
Everything on the
website is free.

00:15:35.680 --> 00:15:38.000
There’s no ads, no
corporate sponsorship.

00:15:38.000 --> 00:15:41.200
It’s strictly non-commercial.
I’m not selling anything.

00:15:41.200 --> 00:15:44.560
I just put it up as a public service,
as a labor of love,

00:15:44.560 --> 00:15:47.440
as a tribute to my grandmother,

00:15:47.440 --> 00:15:53.840
whose own life was saved
with evidence-based nutrition.

